 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Gandalf the Grey: Izzet Wizards",
 "notes": [
  "Nov 19, 2026: main list replaced with his actual sleeved deck (bulk Wizards), trimmed from 119 cards to 100: one copy each of Artisan of Forms, Captain of the Mists, Benthic Criminologists, Kheru Spellsnatcher, Tomik, Izzet Charm and Viashino Pyromancer, plus cuts of Academy Loremaster, Jace's Erasure, Minamo Scrollkeeper, Prism Array, Search the City, Tameshi, Towering-Wave Mystic, Triton Waverider and Urabrask's Anointer. The old Nov 5 list (Bracket 3–4, with the Dualcaster Mage infinites) is retired; its high Bracket 2 form lives on as the Spellslinger B2 version.",
  "Upgrade path: Stage 1 (cards at home) → Stage 2 (cheap spells, ~$7) → Stage 3 (payoffs, ~$16 total) → Spellslinger B2 (interaction and mana, ~$35 total) → Max B2 (best of the old Inalla list, ~$38 total) → the 'adds' list (dollar-plus cards, cheapest first). Each stage includes the ones before it.",
  "Gandalf triggers only on instants and sorceries, choosing a mode not yet chosen: tap or untap, 3 damage to each opponent (4 with Tomik), copy the spell, or put Gandalf on top of the library. Blinking him resets the modes.",
  "Middle kid's must-have: Electrostatic Infantry (first buy, Stage 2). Orko (Delina, Wild Mage) was considered: fun with Wizard enter effects, not a power upgrade; not added."
 ],
